{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>May YHWH bless you and guard you.</b> He placed the blessing first and afterward the guarding, to say that YHWH commands His guarding over them according to the measure and greatness of the blessing. Further, it intends that the greatness of the blessing will be so much that YHWH needs to guard you. Further, it intends <b>May He bless you</b> — and no evil will surround you from the blessing, in the manner of ״פֶּן תֹּאכַל וְשָׂבָעְתָּ״ etc. (Deuteronomy 8:12)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:25.342697971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}